{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And you shall be cleared from this my oath</b> — He did not permit him to take a wife for himself from the daughters of Canaan, but rather that he should be released from the oath, and HaShem, who is good in His eyes, will do. And Rashi wrote (Rashi on Genesis 24:8): he may take a wife for himself from the daughters of Aner, Eshcol, and Mamre. And if they are Canaanites, far be it from him. And in truth they are of the seed of Canaan, for Scripture says (Genesis 14:13) \"Mamre the Amorite, brother of Eshcol and brother of Aner,\" and in Bereshit Rabbah (Bereshit Rabbah 59:8) they said: \"that you shall not take a wife,\" etc. — he warned him concerning the daughters of Canaan, Aner, Eshcol, and Mamre, for it was concerning them that he said \"among whom I dwell,\" for he did not dwell among all the Canaanites, for they were many peoples, but he warned concerning these, the men of his covenant, and all the more so concerning the others. But \"and you shall be cleared from this my oath\" means that he should be released, and Abraham, who knows Isaac the righteous one, knows that he will heed his father and that he will be careful regarding them, and he will go for himself to Ishmael or to Lot and the rest of the peoples. And it is possible that \"this my oath\" alludes to what he said, \"and you shall take a wife for my son from there,\" for perhaps the oath was upon everything, and he would not be alluding to what he said to him, \"you shall not take a wife for my son from the daughters of the Canaanite\" — and this is the meaning of \"this.\" Therefore the servant said, \"and I will turn to the right or to the left\" (Genesis 24:49), and did not say, \"I will return to my master.\""], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "The pronoun 'him' in 'he did not permit him' refers to Abraham not permitting his servant; 'for himself' refers to the servant taking a wife, following Rashi's reading that Abraham releases the servant from the oath if the woman refuses, allowing the servant to take a local wife for himself."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:33:56.532061554Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}